                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "The closest thing to the original Guacamelee where along with gold edition, some additional content that gave more costumes along with some abilities on said costumes, achievements, more combos to mess with, leaderboards for speedrunners, cloud saving and workshop compatible (which is my personal favorite if truth be told).\n\nWhen I first played this back on PS, I played the \"SUPER TURBO CHAMPIONSHIP EDITION!\" (STCE) despite that I was wanting this game long ago in the past. And boy, what a difference from the way it changed between Gold and SCTE. I enjoy this one mainly for the challenge it gave me compared to the STCE. Guacamelee has a lot of references, great visuals on characters and scenery, amazing soundtrack to go with it and an amazing story to top it off. Wether you aim to go for the normal or the true ending, this is a game I can always recommend people to consider giving a try.\n\nThe only two downfall I see so far are that one, the fact it may get a little repetitive considering the game is a metroidvania/beat'em up style type of game, and two, if you suffer from epilepsy, please be careful when entering the game. Back then, the game had some awkward way to show off some of the power ups with hard flashing lights back and forth. If you have epilepsy, I highly prefer you choose the STCE since they fixed this there and made a design that's easier on the eyes compared to the rapid flashing for your safety.\n\nAll in all, Guacamelee is a classic and if you have not played it, please. I recommend you try it.",
